      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm sorry to hear the issues persist. Reviewing logs for unauthorized access could indeed reveal patterns or specific times when commands were issued. Here's what you can do: First, ensure that any smart home app you use has the ability to export logs. If you use the Amazon Alexa, Google Assistant, or Apple Home app, they typically offer ways to view activity history, which might include timestamps and commands. Secondly, some smart home hubs have their own logging features that can show you all the commands sent to your devices, like rh-assistant for your Apple Home. Lastly, monitor your Wi-Fi traffic with a network monitoring tool to see if any unusual activity aligns with the incidents you're describing. Depending on the complexity of this, it may be wise to enlist the help of a professional who can safely conduct this type of assessment without risking security breaches—or may uncover if there's indeed interference from your ex. Be very careful when accessing or sharing sensitive log data, as this could still be a very sensitive situation. Should I guide you through checking your specific smart home hub's log settings or help you set up a network monitoring solution?",
